{{Quote|Only petty criminals get sent to Wobani. No one from that sludge hole could possibly be that important.|Jory of the [[Red Flight (Rebel Alliance)|Red Flight]]|<ref name="Battlefront" />}}
'''Wobani''' was a [[Temperature|temperate]]<ref name="Leia" /> [[planet]]<ref name="Rebel Rising" /> partially hidden by a swirling dust cloud,<ref name="Rogue One" /> located in the [[Wobani system]],<ref name="Battlefront" /> in the [[Bryx sector]]<ref name="RO World Locations" /> of [[the galaxy]]'s [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim]].<ref name="Visual Guide" /> During the [[Imperial Era]], the planet was used by the [[Galactic Empire]] as a site for labor and prison camps.<ref name="Rogue One" />

==Description==
Wobani was covered in a thick cloud of space dust that rarely provided a glimpse through the atmosphere. Wobani's canyons were home to [[Imperial Detention Center & Labor Camp LEG-817]].<ref name="Rebel Rising" />

==History==
{{Quote|Congratulations. You are being rescued. Please do not resist.|[[K-2SO]], to Jyn Erso|<ref name="Rogue One" />}}
When [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] was sixteen, she went on a humanitarian mission to Wobani as part of her [[Challenge of the Heart]], with the intention of providing the people there with supplies. Upon her arrival, she realized how truly terrible the natives were being treated, and decided to take as many [[refugee]]s back to [[Alderaan]] as she could. She was able to trick the [[Tedam|Imperial officer]], [[Major]] [[Tedam]], in charge of Wobani, by hiring several Wobani citizens to come work aboard her ship, rescuing 100 refugees in the process. These refugees were then taken to Alderaan, where they could choose to stay or live on other planets, all at the expense of the [[House of Organa|royal family]]. Unbeknownst to the princess at the time however, in doing this she had undermined negotiations her father, [[Bail Prestor Organa|Bail Organa]], [[Senator]] [[Mon Mothma]] and some of his other allies in the [[Imperial Senate]] had been in for resettlement of the Wobani population for [[Standard month|months]]. Due to the princess's actions the deal could no longer happen as everyone with authority over Wobani was embarrassed, angry and unwilling to bargain.<ref name="Leia" />

Wobani continued to deteriorate under Imperial rule until the Empire elected to only use the planet as a site for manual labor and prisoners.<ref name="The Princess and the Scoundrel">''[[The Princess and the Scoundrel]]''</ref> Shortly before [[Battle of Scarif|stealing]] the [[Death Star plans|plans]] for the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]], [[Jyn Erso]] was held in an [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[Imperial Detention Center & Labor Camp LEG-817|labor camp]] on Wobani<ref name="Rogue One" /> for six [[Standard month|months]]<ref name="Rebel Rising">''[[Rebel Rising]]''</ref> until being [[Liberation of Erso|broken out]]<ref name="Rogue One" /> by [[Extraction Team Bravo]] of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]].<ref name="Battlefront" /> In [[3 ABY]],<ref name="OutlawsDate">{{OutlawsDate}}</ref> a [[transport]] [[shuttle]] traveled from Wobani to the [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim]] [[planet]] [[Kijimi]] where it requested priority landing clearance.<ref name="Outlaws">''[[Star Wars Outlaws]]''</ref>

{{Planet-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The word "Wobani" is an anagram of [[Obi-Wan Kenobi|Obi-Wan (Kenobi)]]. Wobani first appeared in the [[2016]] [[Star Wars Anthology Series|film]] ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]'', which was released on [[December 16]].<ref name="Director Announced">{{SW|url=news/gareth-edwards-and-gary-whitta-onboard-for-star-wars-stand-alone-film|text=Gareth Edwards and Gary Whitta Onboard for ''Star Wars'' Stand-Alone Film}}</ref>

